==Battleground==
*1 [[St. Pigge the 2nd]] spawns.
*Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn, delay 21.33~32 seconds<sup>640f~960f</sup>.
*5 [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 28~36 seconds<sup>840f~1,080f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Fireworks Guys (High-Yield)]] spawn, delay 20.67~24 seconds<sup>620f~720f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Fireworks Guys (Low-Yield)]] spawn, delay 18~21.33 seconds<sup>540f~640f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[THE SLOTH]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[J.K. Bun Bun]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn, delay 43.33~52.67 seconds<sup>1,300f~1,580f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Use the start to build up cash and upgrade worker cat. When the base is hit, try to lure J.K. Bun Bun away from THE SLOTH to burst him down independently. Aim to immobilize J.K. Bun Bun with units such as [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] or [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]]. Then, nuke it down with [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]. Once the J.K. Bun Bun is dead, focus on eliminating THE SLOTH. It should not be able to push very much due to its slow attack rate, however, be mindful of the supporting Traitless peons. Certain units such as [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Teacher BearCat]], [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]], [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]], and [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Glass Cat]] can speed up this process if aiming for the timed score rewards.

On higher crowned difficulties, obtaining the timed score rewards (specifically the Rare Ticket) can be quite difficult even with specialized units. This is because J.K. Bun Bun can have up to 1.2 million health, where THE SLOTH has up to 1.8 million health ({{4c}}), acting as a barrier that prevents most units from getting past ({{4c}} also prevents any unit other than Special and Rare Cats to be deployed, meaning the amount of viable units is greatly reduced). Therefore, it is not realistic to achieve a score higher than 4000 in higher crowned difficulties, but is a nice reward for more experienced and progressed players.

